  "step_3": "The decision reason requires (1) computing an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes, (2) evaluating which outcomes exceed this level, and (3) preferring the lottery with the higher chance of exceeding it. The individual does not mention or imply any such calculation. There is no reference to a comparison point (like 2333.33 Euros), nor any evaluation of outcomes as 'above' or 'below' a reference. Instead, the individual justifies the choice based on the certainty of receiving a guaranteed (albeit lower) amount. This reasoning aligns more with risk aversion or a certainty effect rather than an aspiration-level rule based on mean outcomes. While both the reason and the individual prefer Lottery B, the underlying justification differs fundamentally. The match in choice does not imply use of the same reason. Therefore, there is no evidence the individual used the aspiration-level rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
